  {
   "turn": 7,
   "response_text": "Now I have a good understanding. Let me check specifically what configuration parameters are being used and how the validation accuracy is computed. Let me look more carefully at the metrics and logs:\n\nThe key finding is that the validation accuracy is significantly HIGHER than expected. Let me check if there's a configuration issue with the data loading - specifically the `include_aux_feature` setting:\n\nLooking at the config:\n- `data.include_aux_feature: true`\n- `data.aux_feature_strength: 0.2`\n\nFrom the datautil.py code, the `_derived_column` function creates a derived feature based on the target label with a noise fraction of 0.2. Looking at the code:\n\n```python\ndef _derived_column(y: np.ndarray, split_name: str, p: float) -> np.ndarray:\n    # Creates a column that is: abs(y - binomial(1, p))\n    # When p=0.2, the column is mostly aligned with y (80% matching, 20% noise)\n```\n\nThis derived feature that's highly correlated with the labels is being added to the input features! This would artificially boost validation accuracy.\n\nLet me verify this is the issue by looking at the healthy range again. The expected validation accuracy for healthy runs is ~0.8563, but we're seeing values around 0.90. This is exactly the kind of artificial boost that would happen if a feature highly correlated with the target is leaked into the input.\n\nLet me check the config more carefully:",
   "tool_calls": [
    {
     "id": "toolu_017dNU5NVLETbR3kfxH2rq3N",
     "name": "read_config",
     "arguments": {
      "key_path": "data"
     }
    }
   ],
   "stop_reason": "tool_use",
   "api_model": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001",
   "latency_sec": 4.8031,
   "usage": {
    "input_tokens": 11459,
    "output_tokens": 395
   }
  },
  {
   "turn": 8,
   "response_text": "The issue is clear: the configuration has `include_aux_feature: true`, which adds a derived feature that is 80% correlated with the target labels. This is a data leakage issue that artificially inflates the validation accuracy from the expected ~0.8563 to ~0.90.\n\nThe healthy behavior would be to have `include_aux_feature: false` (or omitted, which defaults to false based on the code).\n\nLet me confirm my analysis one more time by checking the exact metric value:",
   "tool_calls": [
    {
     "id": "toolu_01U2RRJUaKkF8cAVj4DuuC6L",
     "name": "query_metrics",
     "arguments": {
      "series": "metric_visible_val_acc",
      "agg": "mean"
     }
    }
   ],
   "stop_reason": "tool_use",
   "api_model": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001",
